  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The works to which this consent relates, must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of this consent.\r\nReason: To accord with the provisions of Section 18(1) of the Planning (Listed Buildings and Conservation areas) Act 1990.\r\n",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans, documents and specifications: \r\nDrawing Numbers:\r\nDrawings 250119-1150(Rev.P02), 1101(Rev.P03), 1102(Rev.P03), 1103(Rev.P04), 1105(Rev.P03), 1606(Rev.P01), 1600(Rev.P02), 1601(Rev.P02), 1602(Rev.P02), 1603(Rev.P02), 1205(Rev.P01), 1200(Rev.P02), 1201(Rev.P03), 1202(Rev.P02), 1203(Rev.P03), 1204(Rev.P03), 1306(Rev.P02), 1304(Rev.P02), 1305(Rev.P02), 1307(Rev.P02), 1361(Rev.P01), 1362(Rev.P01), 1310(Rev.P01), 1320(Rev.P01), 1330(Rev.P01), 1340(Rev.P01), 1350(Rev.P01), 1360(Rev.P01), 1900(Rev.P01), 1901(Rev.P01), 1902(Rev.P02), 1903(Rev.P01), 1904(Rev.P01), 1507(Rev.P04), 1514(Rev.P04), 1515(Rev.P04), 1516(Rev.P04), 1510(Rev.P02), 1520(Rev.P02), 1540(Rev.P02), 1570(Rev.P02), 1700(Rev.P01), 1701(Rev.P01), 1403(Rev.P05), 1405(Rev.P10), 1406(Rev.P06), 1409(Rev.P07) and 1410(Rev.P04), Drawings 2250096-EGY-ZZ-00-DR-CV-0001(Rev.P02), 0002(Rev.P03) and 1000(Rev.P03), Drawings 2250096-EGY-ZZ-ZZ-DT-CV-3000(Rev.P01), 3001(Rev.P01), 3002(Rev.P01) and 3003(Rev.P01), Drawings ATLD-250119-LP01(Rev.P04), LP02(Rev.P04), LP03(Rev.P04) and LP04(Rev.P04), Drawings 226015-S050(Rev.P1), S090(Rev.P2), S100(Rev.P3), S110(Rev.P3), S120(Rev.P3), S130(Rev.P3), S350(Rev.P1) and SK01(Rev.P1), and infiltration testing drawing (HP01), received 26/08/2026.\r\nSupporting Documents:\r\nBiodiversity Net Gain Assessment (7 September 2026) and Statutory Biodiversity Metric document, received 07/09/2026.\r\nPreliminary Ecological Appraisal (Rev.2.0, 2 September 2026), received 02/09/2026.\r\nAcoustic Report (Issue 3, 21 August 2026), Arboricultural Impact Assessment and Method Statement (May 2026), Archaeological Desk Based Assessment (July 2026), Building Fabric Repair Report (Rev.P2, 20 July 2026), Energy and Sustainability Statement (Issue 1.0, April 2026), Fire Strategy Report (Rev.01, 19 May 2025), Heritage Impact Assessment (August 2026), Phase 1 Ground Condition Assessment (Rev.0, July 2020), Planning Res",
    "Condition : 3 - This consent does not permit the demolition or dismantling of any part of the building, or the removal of any internal/external feature, floor, wall or ceiling surface, except in so far as the alterations hereby approved necessitate the removal of certain parts of the existing structure as specifically shown on the approved drawings.\r\nReason: To protect and preserve the character of the listed building.\r\n",
    "Condition : 4 - The development hereby approved insofar as it relates to repairs and infill of the main house shall, as far as practically possible, be carried out with the re-use of the original bricks (both whole and part bricks), in accordance with the approved method statement. No alternatives shall be used until approval has been given in writing by the local planning authority of a sample panel of 0.5m2 utilising the new brick.\r\nThe use of any new brick shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details.\r\nReason: In order to safeguard the special architectural and historic interest of the listed building.\r\n",
    "Condition : 5 - The timber treads and mouldings and the outer stringer skirting shall, where possible, be salvaged and reinstated on the new stair frame.  \r\nReason: In order to safeguard the special architectural and historic interest of the listed building.\r\n",
    "Condition : 6 - No development above ground level shall take place until full details and samples of all materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the development hereby permitted have been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority. Details must include a detailed schedule of materials, a photographic sample board and rendered drawings, elevations and sections at a sufficient scale (1:20 or 1:50) to illustrate how all external materials will appear together. The submitted information should cover the following elements:\r\n(a)\tBrick/stonework (including brick, stone, masonry, brick panels, feature brick panel, brick framing feature and mortar on-site sample panel, minimum one metre by one metre) including all mortar colours, joint type, brick bond;\r\n(b)\tAny cladding materials / render (including specifications);\r\n(c)\tTiles / roof covering; including parapet coping / capping materials, dormers and canopies;\r\n(d)\tWindow types; and sectional drawings of reveals / courses / sills / textures / head details \r\n(e)\tBalustrading treatment for proposed ramped access (including details / sections / materials); \r\n(f)\tAny boundary treatment that may be required; and \r\n(g)\tAny other materials/details / fittings to be used (including solar panels, heat pumps, extract vents, rainwater goods, boiler flues etc.), with sections and on-site samples where appropriate.\r\nThe development shall then be carried out in accordance with the approved details and maintained as such thereafter.\r\nReason: In order to protect the setting of the listed building and the appearance of the conservation area.\r\n"
  ],
